Fix three correctness issues in the C++ backend: datatype values now print as `Typename.Ctor(fields)` (previously `print` of a datatype failed to compile), collections print with the same braces/separators as the other backends (`{a, b}`, `map[k := v]`), map literals with a duplicate key keep the last value, and codatatypes are now rejected cleanly at declaration instead of crashing the compiler.
